  "name": "dead-time-noise",
  "$comment": "J-EX9 example: a first-order process with dead time (K = 1, tau = 1 s, 0.2 s TransportDelay) under a 10 ms discrete PI (Kp = 2, Ti = 1 s, +-5 limits) whose command reaches the process through a 2-sample IntegerDelay (communication delay). The measurement adds seeded normal noise (std 0.02, seed 42, 1 ms clock), the counter-based stream that the exported FMU reproduces bit for bit. The setpoint steps to 1 at 0.5 s; the process cannot respond before 0.5 + 0.02 + 0.2 = 0.72 s.",
